    "video_URYbRD": {
      "type": "video",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_nqL7yx": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why Flange Fit Matters for Successful Pumping",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "heading_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_q6Rnyn": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The right flange size can make all the difference in your pumping success. If your flange is too small, it can pinch, restrict milk flow, and potentially cause nipple pain. If it’s too large, it may not create a vacuum seal, resulting in reduced suction and inefficient pumping.</p><p>With Ameda’s CustomFit Breast Pump Flanges™ and Universal Soft Breast Pump Flange Inserts, you can customize your fit to maximize comfort and pumping efficiency. A secure yet gentle flange tunnel helps position your nipple without drawing in excess breast tissue or ducts. Comfortable pumping sessions are more productive and less stressful, making it easier to meet your breastfeeding goals.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_nqL7yx",
        "text_q6Rnyn"
      ],
      "custom_css": [
